A while back I posted a little bug I'd noticed.  I've modified my
version of nethack to print a list of genocided monsters.  Sometimes,
before I'd actually genocided anything, I noticed that oracles had
been genocided.  I thought at the time that it must be some kind of 
bug.

Recently, I noticed that as soon as I met the oracle, the game 
genocided them.  I've now figured out the reason for this.  It's
just a little kludge to prevent more than one oracle from being
created.  In fact it happens for any unique monster.  In 
makemon.c:

        /* if it's unique, don't ever make it again */
        if (ptr->geno & G_UNIQ) ptr->geno |= G_GENOD;

Sometime, I may fix up my routine so it will not list monsters
genocided by this.


By the way, shouldn't the oracle be given the power to ZOT you?
Just occured to me.

